              <li><strong>Select PicoRV32 when:</strong> You require a tiny, battle-tested, standard-compliant embedded RISC-V microcontroller with formally proven correctness (SymbiYosys), native AXI/Wishbone interfacing, and sufficient throughput (~0.90 CoreMark/MHz) to run lightweight RTOS kernels.</li>
              <li><strong>Select DarkRISCV when:</strong> You are targeting low-cost Xilinx, Lattice, or Gowin FPGAs where distributed LUT-RAM is free and you want the highest possible instructions-per-cycle (CPI ~1.64) within a sub-10 kGE envelope.</li>
