            <p class="schematic-caption">
              <strong>Figure 2.4:</strong> Ibex decouples execution into two concurrent stages. A 2-entry prefetch buffer in Stage 1 sustains continuous instruction feed over the Open Bus Interface (OBI). Because Stage 2 decodes and executes back-to-back arithmetic instructions in a single cycle with register writeback at the cycle boundary, Ibex achieves near-unity CPI without needing silicon-costly operand bypass networks. Taken branches incur strictly 1 clock cycle of penalty.
