        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Similarity 2 -->
      <div class="sim-card sim-mmode">
        <div class="sim-header">
          <span class="sim-num num-purple">02</span>
          <h4>Machine-Mode (M-Mode) Privileged Control &amp; CSRs</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="sim-lead">
          All evaluated cores operate natively in Machine Mode (M-mode), the mandatory hardware root privilege tier:
        </p>
        <div class="sim-points-stack">
          <div class="sim-point-row">
            <span class="point-badge">Standard Trap Registers</span>
            <span class="point-desc"><code>mstatus</code> (interrupt enable bits), <code>mtvec</code> (trap vector base address), <code>mepc</code> (exception return PC), <code>mcause</code> (trap etiology identifier), and <code>mtval</code>.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="sim-point-row">
            <span class="point-badge">Instrumentation Counters</span>
            <span class="point-desc">64-bit hardware cycle counter (<code>mcycle</code>) and retired instruction counter (<code>minstret</code>), read via standard <code>rdcycle</code> and <code>rdinstret</code> pseudoinstructions.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="sim-point-row">
            <span class="point-badge">Deterministic Trap Vectoring</span>
            <span class="point-desc">Support for direct trap vectoring or vectored mode for timer, software, and external interrupts.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Similarity 3 -->
      <div class="sim-card sim-abi">
        <div class="sim-header">
          <span class="sim-num num-yellow">03</span>
          <h4>Unified Toolchain &amp; Software ABI Portability</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="sim-lead">
          A single C firmware binary compiled with the open standard GNU toolchain runs on any of the evaluated cores:
        </p>
        <div class="sim-points-stack">
          <div class="sim-point-row">
            <span class="point-badge">Calling Convention (ILP32 / ILP32E)</span>
            <span class="point-desc">Function arguments passed in <code>a0&ndash;a7</code>, return values in <code>a0/a1</code>, saved registers in <code>s0&ndash;s11</code>, and stack pointer <code>sp</code> kept 16-byte aligned.</span>
