        <p class="schematic-caption">
          <strong>Figure 5.1:</strong> Empirical benchmark performance spectrum across 17 evaluated 32-bit RISC-V scalar microarchitectures compiled with GCC <code>-O3 -funroll-loops</code> under cycle-accurate Verilator, CXXRTL, Icarus Verilog, and GHDL harnesses. Bars are color-coded by microarchitectural archetype: Coral (Bit-Serial &amp; Multi-Cycle), Cyan (2-Stage Decoupled Harvard), Lilac (3-Stage to 5-Stage Pipelined), and Amber (Dual-Issue / SMT Superscalar). The secondary ink bar indicates Dhrystone DMIPS/MHz. Ibex with branch prediction achieves the peak scalar CoreMark score (3.23 CoreMark/MHz), followed closely by CV32E40P (3.19) and Hazard3 (3.17), while CVA5 (0.87 CPI) and VeeR EL2 (1.03 CPI) lead instruction throughput.
        </p>
